course: dictionary
lesson: 8071
title: Reliance: depending on something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reliance is a noun. It means needing someone or something, or depending on it to help you. Sometimes it also means trust that someone or something will help. You can say «reliance on friends» when you count on your friends, or «reliance on fossil fuels» when a country needs coal, oil and gas to run.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The country has a heavy reliance on imports.» Imports are goods bought from other countries, so reliance here means depending on those goods. Try your meaning in the sentence: depending on imports still makes sense.
explain: Reliance can be good or bad. «Self-reliance» means doing things by yourself. «Over-reliance» means depending on something too much, like «too much reliance on calculators». Look for the small word that changes the meaning: over- means too much, and self- means your own.
explain: The Bible has a line about reliance: «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble» (Proverbs 25:19). Counting on someone who lets you down when you need them hurts, just as a broken tooth or a lame foot would. It is a painful way to find out who can be trusted.
fact: Reliance is a noun, and it is uncountable: you do not say "a reliance" or "reliances".
fact: Reliance means needing or depending on someone or something.
fact: «Reliance on friends» means trusting that your friends will help you.
fact: «Over-reliance» means depending on something too much, and «self-reliance» means depending on yourself.
fact: Some common phrases are «reliance on fossil fuels» and «reliance on imports», which are used in science and geography lessons.
exercise: «The country had a heavy reliance on imports.» What does reliance mean here? | Owning many ships and harbours | *Depending on goods from other countries | Refusing to buy anything from abroad | Making its own food and clothes at home
exercise: «Too much reliance on calculators can stop you practising your sums.» What does too much reliance mean? | Never trusting a calculator at all | Breaking calculators in class | Using calculators only for big sums | *Depending on calculators more than you should
exercise: Which word means doing things by yourself, using your own skills? | Self-timer | Self-defence | *Self-reliance | Self-portrait
test: «She put her reliance on her best friend to keep the secret.» What does reliance mean here? | Keeping the secret from her friend | *Trusting that her friend will help and keep the secret | Forgetting the secret completely | Telling everyone the secret
test: What does «over-reliance on screens» mean? | Using screens for only a short time | Breaking the screens by accident | *Depending on screens too much | Watching a film about screens
exam: «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble.» What does the verse suggest? | *Counting on someone who lets you down in hard times hurts | Trust always makes trouble easier to bear | A lame foot is the best help in trouble | Teeth and feet need care to stay strong
